+# Armino mailbox IPC authority import
+
+`authority/` is the CPU0/CP Armino import and `authority_ap/` is the CPU1/AP
+variant. Their `mailbox_channel.c`, `mb_chnl_buff.c`, and `mb_ipc.c` sources
+are kept as authority modules; neither role is replaced with a Vela state
+machine.
+
+`bk_mailbox_rpmsg.c` is the only Vela-specific lower boundary. It serializes
+the authority `mailbox_data_t` four-word command over the existing RPTUN/RPMsg
+link, copies `mb_ipc` payload bytes, reconstructs a receiving-local pointer,
+and calls the registered authority callback. Mailbox v2 remains RPTUN's
+doorbell only. No new raw shared-SRAM region is allocated.
+
+The transport accepts at most 4096 copied payload bytes per authority command
+and fragments them into 384-byte RPMsg frames. A received payload stays in an
+adapter-owned slot until the corresponding authority IPC response has been
+snapshotted for transmission; it is not released by the immediate physical
+channel ACK.
