+# Armino mailbox IPC over RPMsg
+
+The `authority/` and `authority_ap/` directories preserve the role-specific
+Armino `mailbox_channel.c`, `mb_chnl_buff.c`, and `mb_ipc.c` state machines.
+`bk_mailbox_rpmsg.c` is the Vela-only backend. It serializes the authority
+four-word command over the existing RPTUN/RPMsg connection, copies payloads,
+and reconstructs a receiver-visible payload address before invoking the
+authority callback.
+
+Mailbox v2 remains the RPTUN doorbell; this module does not allocate a raw
+shared-SRAM region or bypass RPTUN. A payload is retained until the matching
+authority IPC response is snapshotted, rather than being released by the
+immediate mailbox-channel ACK.
